My third ascension, the other two were V and W. Failed to do a
hat trick, though, played some Monks, Rangers and
Archeologists in between this and the second one. Got a little
bored and stopped playing, but after reinstalling the OS in
the middle of this week decided to play a game - and here it
goes.

No conducts worth mentioning, lots of mess-ups.

A figurine on Dlvl:1 yielded a tame grid bug, that I didn't
use anyway, leaving both pets behind after finding a coaligned
altar on Dlvl:2.

Soon after that found a tin and opened it. Smelled like dogs.
"Um," I thought, "wasn't there something special about dogs?
Ah, never mind..." Uh oh, bad idea, - spent the rest of the
game aggravating monsters. Not that it mattered much.

Wore a pair of cursed gauntlets by mistake, and that was a
mixed blessing 'cause those were GoPs.

First artifact gift was Snickersnee, which, of course, was a
big disappointment, but the second one was much-desired
(especially for archeologists) Grayswandir. Couldn't find
an uncursed mattock for a long time, so ended up never using
one, - I already had both Grayswandir and some shield when
I stumbled upon one, so pick axe was obviously better for me.

Minetown temple was coaligned, but I didn't use it until
later in the game, since I've got 4 points of protection by
praying for holy water.

Whatever was in Sokoban I've found the other soko-item at
about the same time.

Haven't seen any smoky potions, then dipped unihorn into
sicknesses, and fruit juices turned out to be smoky. Pulled
a wish off the first batch, went on a GDSM.

Mine's End was Catacombs.

Couldn't do the Quest outright, but found a PoGL soon after
leaving for the main dungeon. Fell through a trap door right
next to the Minion of Huhetotl. He was a wimp, anyway.

No Big Room this time, either.

The RNG was unusually cooperative, providing most of my AK
even before the Castle. A cockatrice nest was especially
helpful in this regard. Some throne room provided a genocide
for disenchanters, and I also genocided hs with some random
drop scroll of genocide.

Dlvl:16 had a coaligned temple, which became my base of
operations.

Around Dlvl:20 found a portal to Fort Ludios.

Medusa (Swamp) was trivial, and so was the Castle. Some nice
stuff in store rooms, the WoW was (0:3) I think: CoP, and
four magic markers, saved the last two wishes for an
emergency.

Lots of genocides and enchant armours.

Reverse genocide for nurses was an utter failure: I didn't
get a single point off six or seven nurses (though getting
'I hope you don't mind' message). Must be a bug or something.
Reverse genocide for wraiths got me a few levels, though.

Btw, the char was almost pure melee; enhanced divination by
casting some 'detect monsters', but never used a spell other
than that and getting myself confused with forgotten spells.

Gehennom, um, was Gehennom, and I was stubborn enough to
explore it fully, and didn't even use my heap of magic maps.

Sacrificial orgy on Dlvl:16 ended in me sacrificing some
human, converting an altar and losing protection. Luckily,
the gold the priest carried was enough to get it all back at
Minetown.

Forgot to put on teleport control after dealing with Rodney,
so ended up on Dlvl:2 instead of Dlvl:49. Didn't even realize
what went wrong, but managed to recover.

Moloch's Sanctum: conflict+two wands of death.

Back to Dlvl:1: scrolls and wands of teleport.

Planes: conflict.

Astral Plane: somehow I couldn't tin Famine, and Death took me
from 511 to 495 hp. I was so annoyed I didn't hunt for
Pestilence, just sacrificed the amulet at Death's altar (in
the centre) and wrote this post.

